node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store

# Local tooling state, not part of the project
.atl/
# One developer's Codex verbosity preference. `.codex/hooks.json` and the continuation
# note beside it *are* committed — they are shared. This one is a machine setting, and it
# refused a worktree run for being uncommitted, which is the right behaviour applied to
# the wrong file.
.codex/config.toml

# Working documents that predate the public repository
agent-flow-implementation-spec.md
agent-flow-mvp1-plan.md

# agent-flow's own run state, when used on itself
.agent-flow/runs/
.agent-flow/cache/
.agent-flow/current-run

# Playwright's per-run output. The baselines under
# apps/web/visual/__screenshots__ are committed; this is the scratch space
# where a failing run writes its actual and diff images.
apps/web/visual/.results/
apps/web/e2e/.results/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/test-results/

# Packaging smoke output: a tarball and the throwaway prefix it is installed into.
.packaging/
*.tgz

# The packaging smoke renames the checkout's dashboard bundle aside to prove the
# packaged server is not reading it, and restores it afterwards. A run killed at the
# wrong moment leaves this behind; it is a build artifact, not a loss.
apps/web/dist.hidden-by-packaging-smoke/

# The design system itself is committed: PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md, .impeccable/design.json
# and the detector's shared ignores are meant to be read and argued with in a review.
# These three are not part of it — they are per-machine state: dedup cache and pending
# queue for the per-edit hook, and one developer's consent and overrides. A shared
# exception that lands in config.local.json is a shared exception nobody else gets.
#
# The installer also writes these to `.git/info/exclude`, which does not travel to a
# clone; here they are, where a second contributor inherits them.
**/.impeccable/hook.cache.json
**/.impeccable/hook.pending.json
**/.impeccable/config.local.json

# Local design mockups
ui/
apps/deck/dist.hidden-by-packaging-smoke/
